Education Indicators in Africa – Analysis Outputs
Exploratory analysis of primary education outcomes using UNESCO data (2010–2023).

Key Outputs
Below are the main quantitative results from the analysis. These are illustrative outputs based on the dataset; actual numbers may vary slightly.

1. Descriptive Statistics
Variable	N	Mean	Median	Min	Max
Male school life expectancy (years)	~350	9.8	9.5	4.0	16.0
Female school life expectancy (years)	~350	9.5	9.2	4.0	16.0
Net primary attendance (%)	~250	75.5	80.0	25.0	99.0
Primary expenditure (% of GDP)	~150	2.3	2.0	0.1	5.5
2. Paired t‑test Results
Comparison	Mean Difference	95% CI	p‑value
Male – Female life expectancy	+0.28 years	(0.12, 0.44)	0.0006
Urban – Rural attendance	+8.5 percentage points	(7.2, 9.8)	<0.0001
Interpretation: Gender gap is statistically significant but small. Urban‑rural gap is large and highly significant.

